{"id": "1.2-00042", "case_id": "opencores_pid32_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "opencores/dsp_core_pid_controller", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00042&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (6 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: RTL/16x16bit_multiplier_pipelined.v, RTL/CLA_fixed.v, RTL/PID.v, RTL/booth.v. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00042&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>4 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00042&amp;file=private%2Freference%2FRTL%2F16x16bit_multiplier_pipelined.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed verification testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>5 verification testpoints:</strong> adder, booth, multiply, pid_sequence, pid_reset. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00042&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00042&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># Implement the signed fixed-width PID controller project\nRead the original project manual and implement every declared module in its\nrequired file. The fixed configuration uses a 32-bit Wishbone data port, 16-bit\nbyte address, signed 16-bit coefficients and inputs, and wrapping 32-bit results.\nThe pinned defines header is expanded privately; no includes are required.\n\nBehavior and timing clarifications:\n- PID reset is active-high asynchronous. The multiplier&#x27;s i_rst is active-low\n  asynchronous. PID uses a 32-bit adder and a pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier.\n- Registers at byte addresses 0,4,8,12,16 are Kp,Ki,Kd,SP,PV, written from low\n  16 bits and sign-extended on reads. Writing Kp or Kd updates Kpd=Kp+Kd (wrap\n  16 bits). Writing PV starts an update. Read-only Kpd,error,negative previous\n  error,u,sigma,overflow are at 20,24,28,32,36,40. Address 44 accepts zero to\n  clear error,u,sigma and overflow, preserving gains/SP/PV. Hardware reset clears all.\n- e=wrap16(SP-PV); previous term=wrap16(-old_e). Then sigma=wrap32(sigma+Ki*e),\n  u=wrap32(Kpd*e+sigma+Kd*previous_term). Coefficients/errors multiply as signed\n  integers. Arithmetic wraps, without saturation or implicit fixed-point shifts.\n- Wishbone requests hold address/data/control until ACK. Writes acknowledge\n  after request registration; write ACK stays high until STB drops. Reads ACK\n  combinationally when the requested register is unlocked. Gain writes/reads\n  and state reads can wait while arithmetic locks are active. No exact internal\n  FSM encoding is required; complete an update within 20 input clocks after PV\n  acceptance. o_valid=1 means output/state are not busy (including reset/idle),\n  not a one-cycle completion pulse. Results hold between updates.\n- Overflow flags are Kpd[0], current error[1], previous error&#x27;s flag[2], u[3],\n  sigma[4]. Kpd/current error flags update on the corresponding calculations;\n  sigma accumulation overflow is sticky, and u includes that sticky flag plus\n  overflow from its two subsequent additions. Reset/RS clears flags.\n- multiplier_16x16bit_pipelined accepts operands whenever i_start=1. Product and\n  o_ready correspond to the previous clock&#x27;s accepted operands: two register\n  stages, one new product each clock under sustained start. Ready carries bubbles.\n  adder_32bit computes the 33-bit unsigned sum including carry-in.\n- booth_radix4 maps triplets 000..111 to digits 0,+1,+1,+2,-2,-1,-1,0 via\n  zero, double(abs digit=2), negation(digit&lt;0). booth_array applies this to eight\n  overlapping radix-4 slices, appending zero below the multiplier&#x27;s LSB.\n  half/full adders and compressor42 preserve the binary weighted sum (S weight1,\n  carry/cout weight2). Prefix operators A produce bit propagate/generate,\n  B combines two groups, C combines a group with a preceding generate.\n  partial_product_gen emits a 17-bit Booth partial with inverted sign bit, no\n  negation correction bit: complement md when negating, zero when zero-select,\n  sign-extend to 17 bits with inverted sign, and shift once for double, inserting\n  the negation bit at the low end. These utility interfaces remain required.\n\nPrivate points check Booth encoding, carry arithmetic, streamed signed products,\nPID sequences and software reset. Finite tests sample behavior; no universal\nequivalence or exhaustive overflow coverage is claimed. Public checks compile only.\n\nImplement every required path in output_contract.json. Declaration-only ports\nare in interfaces/modules.v. No initial/final, delays, simulation system tasks,\nforce/release or external includes are permitted. Only declared RTL is collected.\nMissing files, forbidden constructs or failed top compilation score zero. Each\nprivate point has equal weight and requires all of its checks to pass. Use\nterminal/file_editor, iverilog, vvp and Python iteratively; finish by saving RTL.\nRun `python3 checks/check.py` for public compilation feedback.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/261b8a907be7e677c5e4db643d312005203cada841c215d26d42561352559d4d.txt", "size": 37031, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case